	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105032723924?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANETs) are increasingly deployed in mission-critical domains such as UAV swarms, military communication, and disaster recovery. The emergence of 5G and forthcoming 6G networks introduces advanced capabilities including ultra-reliable low latency communication (URLLC) and network slicing. However, the inherent challenges of MANETs dynamic topology, mobility-induced route failures, congestion, and energy constraints limit the effectiveness of traditional routing schemes. The aim is to design an adaptive routing framework that ensures reliability, low latency, and energy efficiency for mission-critical MANETs, while seamlessly integrating 5G/6G features. An AI-enabled cross-layer QoS routing framework (AI-CLA-QR) is proposed. The framework leverages a cross-layer telemetry bus that aggregates metrics including buffer occupancy, delay, link quality, energy, and packet velocity. A reinforcement learning-based agent selects the Best Forwarding Node (BFN) to optimize multi-metric QoS objectives. Service differentiation maps real-time data (RTD) to URLLC slices and non-real-time (NRT) flows to enhance mobile broadband (eMBB) slices. Edge intelligence provides policy feedback to dynamically adjust routing priorities. Simulation results demonstrate that AI-CLA-QR improves throughput by up to 25%, increases packet delivery ratio by 15%, reduces end-to-end delay by 23%, lowers deadline miss ratio by 45%, and achieves 20% energy savings compared to AODV, CLAODV, and QRE2PM baselines. The proposed framework ensures robust, QoS-aware, and energy-efficient routing in 5G/6G-integrated MANETs, making it suitable for UAV swarm coordination and other mission-critical applications.  © 2025 IEEE.},
